Lock media element volume to the system volume (WEBKIT_VOLUME_LOCKED).

Fixes "every video starts back at full volume": with WEBKIT_GST_MEDIA_ROLE=
x-maemo (webkit-gst-media-role-env.patch) the hardware volume keys step all
browser PulseAudio streams via module-meego-mainvolume — but each new <video>
element creates a NEW pulse stream, and WebKit pushes the element's JS volume
(el.volume, 1.0 for a fresh element — and YouTube's player sets it on every
video load) down onto that stream as an explicit per-stream volume
(HTMLMediaElement::updateVolume -> MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer::setVolume ->
playbin -> pulsesink). Device-proven: at mainvolume step 4 (44%) a new x-maemo
stream WITHOUT a client volume inherits 44%, while one connecting WITH an
explicit 100% client volume plays at 100% — so navigating to the next video
resets loudness to full until the user touches the volume keys again.

Upstream already has the right model for phones: m_volumeLocked — what iPhones
use (defaultVolumeLocked() is true on iOS small-screen). When locked, page JS
writes to el.volume are ignored for playback (the setVolume locked path never
calls updateVolume, so nothing is ever stamped on the pulse stream), el.volume
instead MIRRORS the player/stream volume, and mute keeps working — the system
volume (hardware keys / mainvolume) is the single owner of loudness, and every
new stream inherits it. This patch makes that default reachable off-iOS via
WEBKIT_VOLUME_LOCKED=1 (set in deploy/runtime-common.sh). Unset/0 = upstream
behaviour.
--- a/Source/WebCore/html/HTMLMediaElement.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/html/HTMLMediaElement.cpp
@@ -151,6 +151,7 @@
 #include "VisibilityAdjustment.h"
 #include "WebCoreJSClientData.h"
 #include <JavaScriptCore/Uint8Array.h>
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include <limits>
 #include <pal/SessionID.h>
 #include <ranges>
@@ -495,12 +496,20 @@
     return true;
 }

 static bool defaultVolumeLocked()
 {
 #if PLATFORM(IOS)
     return PAL::currentUserInterfaceIdiomIsSmallScreen();
 #else
-    return false;
+    // SFOS: WEBKIT_VOLUME_LOCKED=1 hands loudness to the system volume (the
+    // hardware keys / module-meego-mainvolume), the iPhone model: page JS
+    // el.volume writes don't touch the PulseAudio stream volume, so a new
+    // stream per video can't reset it back to 100%. Unset = upstream.
+    static bool locked = []() {
+        const char* env = std::getenv("WEBKIT_VOLUME_LOCKED");
+        return env && *env && *env != '0';
+    }();
+    return locked;
 #endif
 }

